            </div>
            <div style="--c:var(--c-purple)">
              <h3><i></i>Push notifications</h3>
              <p>A change starts the sync when the provider notifies you; a scheduled check catches the rest.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="--c:var(--c-orange)">
              <h3><i></i>Organisation limits</h3>
              <p>Admins cap the detail between work and private calendars.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="--c:var(--c-sky)">
              <h3><i></i>Activity log</h3>
              <p>Runs and changes with counts and codes, never event content.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="--c:var(--c-indigo)">
              <h3><i></i>EU data location</h3>
              <p>The database and the sync can stay in Cloudflare's EU jurisdiction.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="--c:var(--c-slate)">
              <h3><i></i>Colours</h3>
              <p>A colour per account in the app, and a colour for the blocks it writes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="wrap why">
          <div>
            <h2>Why moved meetings get lost</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              A recurring meeting moved for one week is an exception to its series. Sync tools that
              rebuild copies on a schedule can miss it until the next full run.
            </p>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>slotmirror reads each occurrence of a series, so a moved one keeps its identity.</li>
            <li>It changes only what differs: create, update or delete, never a rebuild.</li>
            <li>Push notifications start the sync when the provider reports the move, not on a timer.</li>
            <li>
              Event contents are read during a sync and kept only in memory, never written to the
              database.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="guides">
